{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795722359,"nonce":"HzyT6DjAGXQEj1m23LEeYZlzk14=","title":"Dispatch at a fork's commit runs the fork's Pipeline without fork limits","message":"Found while designing the MCP Plugin (9130efd, ADR-0086 §9). Dispatch accepts refs/pull/\u003cN\u003e/head and raw SHAs (canonicalize_ref, crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs:8336) and reads the Pipeline at the resolved commit (lib.rs:8441). Fork limits key on Event::PullRequest { fork: true } (crates/scarab-forge/src/lib.rs:835), so a manual or API dispatch at a fork pull request's head runs the fork's own YAML with no fork limits (secrets not tied to an Environment, the OIDC subject, push, a write clone token). Environment allowed_refs still protects Environment secrets.\n\nFix (owner decision 2026-11-27): fork code detection at dispatch.\n- a branch or tag of the repository: the repository's code, as today;\n- refs/pull/\u003cN\u003e/head: fork code when the forge says PR N's head repository is not the base; no answer refuses the dispatch with the reason;\n- a raw commit SHA: fork code, always (a forge serves any fork's commits through the base repository).\nA Run of fork code gets the fork pull request limits whatever started it. Build step 1 of ADR-0086, shipped as a 0.8.x patch.","files":null}]}